// VLFeat's fast_expn (sift.c): exp(-x) by linear interpolation, in double, in
// a 257-entry table of exp(-k * 25 / 256), and 0 from x = 25 on. VLFeat
// returns 0 only above 25 and reads one entry past its table at exactly 25;
// no kernel argument comes near 25.
//
// Why this table and not __expf: __expf is faster (the extraction kernels
// take about 5 % less GPU time with it on ETH3D door) and closer to the true
// exp. But cusift must reproduce COLMAP's VLFeat CPU backend, and VLFeat
// weights its samples with this table, which differs from exp by up to about
// 0.1 %. With __expf, the sample weights differ from VLFeat's by that much, so
// an orientation whose peak is close to 0.8 times the highest peak can be kept
// by one backend and dropped by the other, and the descriptors differ
// slightly. With the table, the median orientation error against VLFeat on
// door drops from 7e-6 to 7e-7 rad.
#define CUSIFT_EXPN_SZ 256
#define CUSIFT_EXPN_MAX 25.0

